WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.020
Recently, China has combined two
practices to make significant political

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:13.440
and territorial gains in Asia without
crossing the threshold into open

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.480
conflict with the United States. First,
since the 1990s, China has focused on

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.580
low-cost ways to disrupt, disable, and
deny US' ability to operate in the region.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.720
Instead of trying to compete directly
with US power projection capabilities,

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.130
China's ballistic and cruise missiles,
for example, hurt the US' ability to

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:36.480
come to the aid of Japan, Taiwan, or the
Philippines in the case of a conflict

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.540
with China. Second, since 2009, instead of
direct confrontation to push the United

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.680
States out of the Asia-Pacific, China has
engaged in activities below the

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.149
threshold of conflict. For example, China
has increased the risk to the United

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:55.140
States of operating in the South China
Sea by harassing US vessels and aircraft

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:00.359
with non-military platforms to maintain
a degree of deniability and discourage a

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:05.400
counter response. As a result, China has
gained more power and territorial

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.080
control in Asia without recourse.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.860
Do you
think the United States should push back

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.820
more against China?
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.479
what other topics you'd like our
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:24.290
sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos and from AEI.

